# Path Dependency CI

RULE: Clone path dependencies to `../repo-name` in CI. pyproject.toml must use `path = "../repo-name"`. Never use `deps/`. Use `${DEP_BRANCH:-main}` or PR label `dep-branch: feat/X` in CI clone steps.
WHY: Local workspace has repos as siblings; CI clone to `../` creates same layout. `deps/` breaks `uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md, 06-coding-standards/dependency-management.md

DO: `git clone -b ${DEP_BRANCH:-main} ... ../repo-name`; `uv pip install --system -e ../repo-name`; `path = "../repo-name"` in pyproject.toml
NEVER: `git clone ... deps/repo-name`; `git clone ... repo-name` (missing ../); clone without branch fallback

Quickmerge creates PR label `dep-branch: feat/X`; CI reads it to clone dep at feature branch. Full YAML/toml examples: CODEX 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md
